<article class="env-remark" id="01KT">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01KT">Remark <span data-tag="01KT">4.6.4.17</span>.</a> Let $F: K \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a morphism of simplicial sets. Then the slice and coslice diagonal morphisms </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{/F} \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\vec{\times }_{ \operatorname{Fun}(K, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) } \{ F\}  \quad \quad \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{F/} \rightarrow \{ F\}  \vec{\times }_{ \operatorname{Fun}(K,\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) } \operatorname{\mathcal{C}} \]
</div>
<p> are monomorphisms of simplicial sets. This follows from Remark <a data-tag="02GJ" href="/tag/02GJ">4.6.4.16</a>, together with the observation that for every simplicial set $J$, the comparison maps </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  c_{J,K}: J \diamond K \twoheadrightarrow J \star K \quad \quad c_{K,J}: K \diamond J \twoheadrightarrow K \star J \]
</div>
<p> are epimorphisms (see Exercise <a data-tag="02GG" href="/tag/02GG">4.6.2.5</a>) </p>
</article>
